# Rebuilding extras (phase 2) against a prefix, and running the torch-free consumer smoke.
# Hand-written (unlike requirements/openvino-*.txt, which are generated from openvino.sh).
#
# PINNING POLICY: pin what we choose, track what upstream chooses.
#
#   ninja   - ours. A build tool nothing else in the environment has an opinion about, so an exact
#             pin costs nothing and makes a silent toolchain change show up as a diff.
#   numpy   - NOT ours to pin. In the AOT jobs it is whatever torch resolves for the pinned
#             ExecuTorch tag; pinning it here would mean editing this file every time the ET pin
#             moves, and losing that race silently reintroduces the drift the pin was meant to
#             prevent. We assert presence and let the ET pin decide the version.
#
# Known and deliberate: openvino==2025.4.1 requires numpy<2.4.0 (tighter than nncf's <2.5.0), so the
# AOT locks resolve numpy 2.3.5 while the torch-free locks resolve 2.5.2. That split is real and is
# now visible as a diff between two committed locks instead of a downgrade buried in a pip log.
#
# TORCH IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT - do not "fix" this by adding it.
# scripts/emit-{openvino,xnnpack}-fixtures.py and extras/lstm/aot/* all import torch, but torch is
# installed by ExecuTorch's own install_executorch.sh, which pins torch==2.13.0 from
# download.pytorch.org and yields a LOCAL-VERSION build (2.13.0+cpu). Compiling that into a lock
# against PyPI resolves a different artifact for the same version string, so the lock would either
# reinstall over ExecuTorch's torch or fail outright - and it would duplicate a pin upstream owns,
# which then has to move in lockstep with every ET pin bump. That is precisely the drift trap the
# generated openvino-*.in files exist to avoid.
#
# The contract this leaves implicit: any job running a torch importer must also run
# install_executorch.sh earlier in the SAME job. Nothing enforces that today. It is the same shape
# as the bug the full-gate split exposed, where full-aot's OpenVINO emitter lost the wheel a step in
# another job used to provide (fixed in 4c74892). A structural guard belongs in
# test/extras_gate_full_split.test.sh's family; until then, treat this paragraph as the contract.
ninja==1.13.0
numpy
